 "B2-029": {
  "case": "inconsistent",
  "conflicts": [
   "\"Tomas works earlier in the day than Nadia\" and \"Nadia is on later than whoever has packing\" create ambiguity with relative ordering depending on packing station assignment; also \"Speaking from memory, Tomas is on intake\" conflicts with \"The people on a station are Lukas, Tomas, Daniel\" implying only three station staff and others are on no station, but later statements about Tomas being between Lukas and Rohan and after one and before the other of Lukas and Rohan create ordering constraints that cannot all be satisfied simultaneously under station assignment; additionally, \"Tomas comes later in the day than Daniel\" and \"Tomas works earlier in the day than Nadia\" and \"Rohan takes over from Nadia later in the day\" imply Nadia precedes Rohan, but \"Nadia is on later than whoever has packing\" and station constraints limit possible packing assignee; multiple statements about Tomas's preferences (13:00, between Lukas and Rohan, not 13:00) contradict; \"Lukas would have been a better fit for the 11:00 block\" is evaluative and not a constraint; inconsistent ordering requirements for Tomas relative to Lukas and Rohan ('fairly sure Tomas is on after one of Lukas and Rohan and before the other') cannot be resolved without clear pairwise constraints; station assignment: only Lukas, Tomas, Daniel can be on stations (intake, calibration, packing), others on no station — but Nadia and Rohan must be assigned to blocks and thus would be on 'no station', which is allowed; however, the phrase \"one person per block\" and \"each person works exactly one block\" means all five staff are scheduled; the conflict arises from contradictory relative time constraints under station and block assignment"
  ]
 },
